```

## Example from Class
While `fork()` is not in your provided notes, it is typically used in a structure similar to this:

```c
#include <unistd.h> // Header for fork()

int main() {
    int pid = fork(); // The process splits here

    if (pid == 0) {
        // This code runs only in the child process
    } else {
        // This code runs only in the parent process
    }
    return 0;
}
```

